        "callout_title": "Why Does My Mouth Burn When I Eat Spicy Food?",
        "callout_text": "Burning can happen when the lining of the mouth is irritated or sensitive. It can have several causes, including OSMF, so burning alone does not confirm the condition. If it keeps returning or occurs with cheek tightness or reduced mouth opening, arrange an assessment.",
        "link_to": "test",
