            "text": "The normal balance between collagen production and breakdown becomes disturbed, allowing dense connective tissue to build up."
          }
        },
        "block_3": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "art": "change-stiff",
            "icon": "lock",
            "tone": "amber",
            "title": "Tissue Becomes Stiff",
            "text": "As fibrosis increases, the normally flexible oral tissues become less elastic and harder to stretch."
          }
        },
        "block_4": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "art": "change-vessels",
            "icon": "vessel",
            "tone": "teal",
            "title": "Small Blood Vessels Are Affected",
            "text": "Fibrotic changes can narrow or reduce small blood vessels, affecting circulation within the tissues."
